13. REFINEMENTS
========================================================================

 13a. Is the 2877.8 Hz / 17.88 m/s line (5.6 sigma) the 48th mains harmonic?
    mains fundamental, fan-on session : 60.0024 Hz -> 48th harmonic at 2880.12 Hz
    mains fundamental, empty-room 60 s: 60.0105 Hz -> 48th harmonic at 2880.50 Hz
    the two 48th harmonics differ by 0.39 Hz = 0.3 FFT bins
    2877.8 Hz sits 2.3 Hz from the fan-on 48th harmonic.
    -> a mains drift of a few mHz moves the 48th harmonic by whole FFT bins, which
       appears as a large per-bin prominence difference between sessions. MAINS,
       not a blade tip. (FINDINGS already lists 2880.76 Hz at 12.3 dB in the
       empty room, with no fan present.)

