========================================================================
14. UPPER BOUND AND INDEPENDENT CROSS-CHECK
========================================================================

 14a. What the -23 dB injection threshold means physically:
    detectable Doppler line rms  = 8.10 uV
    total fan-on IF rms          = 157.6 uV  (ADC LSB = 336 uV, so the line is 41x SMALLER than one LSB)
    line-to-total-IF-power ratio = -25.8 dB
    -> 50 s of coherent averaging buys enough processing gain to see a Doppler line
       far below one ADC code. The fan produced nothing at that level.

 14b. Broadband bound: any broad Doppler wing from the fan
    measured in-band power difference (fan-on minus fan-off, mains notched) = -0.97 dB
    the sign is NEGATIVE, so the limit is set by the session-to-session gain offset
    (fan-on IF rms 157.6 uV vs fan-off 173.6 uV = -0.84 dB, a receiver/session
    difference, not the fan). Any broadband fan contribution is therefore below
    roughly 1 dB of the in-band noise power and cannot be separated from that offset.

 14c. INDEPENDENT CROSS-CHECK: FMCW consecutive-chirp MTI on the fan-on capture,
      using the exact pipeline that scored 12 sigma on the moving person.
